{"title": "Hiring Update: Progress and Outlook", "slides": [
  {
    "title": "Roles Open",
    "bullets": [
      "Product Manager – focused on scaling core features",
      "Data Engineer – to support analytics infrastructure",
      "UX Designer – for improved user journey mapping",
      "DevOps Engineer – to enhance CI/CD pipelines"
    ],
    "notes": "We currently have four key roles open across product, engineering, and experience. Each role aligns with our short-term roadmap priorities and addresses critical gaps in our delivery capacity.",
    "layout": "bullets"
  },
  {
    "title": "Pipeline Status",
    "bullets": [
      "30% of roles have active candidate pipelines",
      "15% in early screening phase with strong fit signals",
      "25% in outreach or sourcing stage",
      "Remaining 30% in pipeline development or refinement"
    ],
    "notes": "Our hiring pipeline is active but unevenly distributed. We’re seeing momentum in the UX and DevOps roles, which are high-impact for user experience and deployment speed. We’ll need to accelerate outreach on the data engineering role.",
    "layout": "bullets"
  },
  {
    "title": "Key Risks",
    "bullets": [
      "Talent scarcity in specialized engineering roles",
      "Delayed hiring could impact Q3 product launch timelines",
      "Limited diversity in current candidate pool",
      "Increased cost if we extend search timelines beyond 60 days"
    ],
    "notes": "We must monitor talent availability closely—especially in niche technical areas. A delay in hiring could ripple into our launch schedule. We’re also reviewing sourcing strategies to improve representation across backgrounds.",
    "layout": "bullets"
  },
  {
    "title": "Next Steps",
    "bullets": [
      "Finalize role descriptions and job specs by end of week",
      "Launch targeted outreach campaigns for engineering roles",
      "Establish a cross-functional hiring review board by [date]",
      "Set weekly check-ins to track pipeline progress"
    ],
    "notes": "We’ll move quickly to finalize job specs and ramp up outreach. The hiring review board will ensure alignment with business goals. Weekly updates will keep leadership informed and allow for agile course corrections.",
    "layout": "bullets"
  }
]}

{"title": "Q3 Design Studio Quarterly Review", "theme": "editorial", "slides": [
  {
    "title": "Key Highlights",
    "bullets": [
      "Launched three new client projects with strong user engagement metrics",
      "Increased average project delivery speed by 15%",
      "Received positive feedback on accessibility improvements in 8 of 10 designs",
      "Expanded our collaboration with two emerging brands in the sustainability space"
    ],
    "notes": "We saw consistent growth in both quality and velocity. Client satisfaction scores rose across all major deliverables. The sustainability focus helped us stand out in competitive markets.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  },
  {
    "title": "Performance Metrics",
    "bullets": [
      "Client retention rate: [insert number]%",
      "Average project revenue: [insert amount]",
      "Design iteration cycles reduced from [insert number] to [insert number] days",
      "New client acquisition: [insert number] in Q3"
    ],
    "notes": "These numbers reflect our improved workflow and client trust. The reduction in iteration time shows better alignment with client needs early in the process.",
    "layout": "title-content"
